{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the Drop-off tech process, the customer is first informed about canceling the order."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly defines the process start (init), explicitly names the initialization action (n1), and details the first substantive task (n2)."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Then, the question arises: has the order already been fulfilled?"
      ],
      "justification": "The question establishes the decision point captured by the XOR branch node, while the action node faithfully restates the query itself."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"Yes,\" the bag is marked as returned in IS."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard captures the affirmative condition driving the branch, and the action captures the resulting state update."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the answer is \"No,\" the script(s) are marked as declined by the customer in IS."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard captures the negative condition driving the branch, and the action captures the corresponding state update."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the bag is marked as returned in IS, the script bag is returned as well."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the follow-up action executed on the positive branch path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, when the script(s) are marked as declined by the customer in IS, the script order is declined."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the follow-up action executed on the negative branch path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the customer notification is processed, and the entire process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "The parallel branch paths must reconvene before the final notification step (n8). The concluding phrase supports both the explicit termination action (n9) and the structural end node (e1)."
    }
  ],
